module lib/skyrme/story_o16
  Oxygen-16 from the SLy5 Skyrme functional, on the first of the two meshes
  of posts/2026-09-25-skyrme-hartree-fock-of-oxygen-16.viv: 150 points of
  0.1 fm, a box 15 fm wide. The post solves again at 0.05 fm and
  extrapolates to zero spacing; one mesh is enough to follow the iteration,
  and it gives the same numbers as the post's numpy twin on that mesh.

<main>  @5c61eb66
  what     Solve for the ground state of $^{16}$O with SLy5 on a mesh of
           spacing SO_H across a box SO_BOX wide, and print the energy per
           nucleon, the radii, the six orbital energies and the number of
           passes. They are the numpy twin's to rounding
           [test "on the 0.1 fm mesh E/A, the radii and the six orbital energies are the numpy twin's to 1e-7"].
  SO_H     $h$  the mesh spacing, fm
  SO_BOX   the width of the box, fm; the densities are zero at its edge
  so_nr    the number of mesh points, SO_BOX / SO_H
  so_res   the result (lib/skyrme/skyrme's SkyrmeO16): E/A (MeV), the
           proton, neutron and charge radii (fm), the neutron $1s_{1/2}$,
           $1p_{3/2}$, $1p_{1/2}$ energies and the proton ones (MeV), the
           number of passes, and the converged densities
